  Persistent reasoning state was initialized for this agent session.

claim current-goal
  Implement `partial_structure` on cattrs' `BaseConverter` plus top-level export, returning a new `PartialResult` type; work on a new branch from main and commit everything.

claim requirements
  - `PartialResult` fields: value (partial object or None), is_complete, structured_fields (frozenset of field names structured from input), failed_fields (frozenset), errors (Exception or None), error_map (dict field name -> Exception).
  - Fields absent from input count as failed, not structured.
  - Failed fields with defaults fall back to defaults; required fields without defaults force value=None.
  - Nested attrs/dataclass fields recurse: partially complete nested -> use its partial value AND mark parent field failed; no nested value possible -> normal field failure.
  - Collection fields (List, Dict) are atomic: element failure fails whole field.
  - `PartialResult.refine(data)` -> new PartialResult fixing failed fields with data, preserving structured fields.
  - init=False fields excluded from structured_fields and failed_fields.
  - forbid_extra_keys: extra keys => is_complete False but value still produced.
  - Respect detailed_validation (aggregate errors into ClassValidationError w/ notes when on; first raw error when off).
  - Support attrs classes, dataclasses, TypedDicts. Export PartialResult from cattrs.

claim current-hypothesis
  Implementation plan (repo is cattrs @ main, Python 3.10+ required, attrs>=25.4):
  1. New module src/cattrs/partial.py defining PartialResult (attrs @define frozen slots, Generic[T]); private fields converter/cl/data (eq=False, repr=False) power refine().
  2. BaseConverter.partial_structure(obj, cl) in converters.py: strip Annotated; TypedDict -> typeddicts helpers (_adapted_fields/_required_keys from gen.typeddicts); attrs/dataclass (non-generic, has()) -> field walk using adapted_fields; everything else -> try full structure() and wrap result.
  3. Field walk: skip init=False; input key = alias if converter.use_alias else name; constructor kwarg = attribute alias; absent -> KeyError failure (+default fallback, fatal if no default); nested complete -> structured; nested partial -> use partial value, parent failed; nested value None -> normal failure; other types atomic via _structure_attribute; detailed_validation attaches AttributeValidationNote and aggregates ClassValidationError; error_map entry for every failed field; is_complete = value is not None and no failed fields and no extra-key violation.
  4. Non-mapping input -> graceful failure result (value None, all init fields failed).
  5. Export PartialResult + partial_structure from cattrs/__init__.py (top-level partial_structure bound to global_converter).
  6. tests/test_partial.py covering all semantics; HISTORY.md entry; docs section.

